1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:06,300
PNC's third quarter: an earnings beat,
the cleanest credit of six peers, and
the thinnest capital.

2
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:12,159
Adjusted earnings per share were
five dollars and nine cents, above
every estimate we found.

3
00:00:12,710 --> 00:00:16,509
Net interest income rose fifteen
percent to four point two one billion

4
00:00:16,509 --> 00:00:18,907
dollars, though revenue missed
slightly.

5
00:00:19,457 --> 00:00:23,939
Net charge-offs of twenty-eight basis
points were the lowest of the six
banks.

6
00:00:24,489 --> 00:00:29,966
CET1 capital of nine point eight
percent ranked last, though well
above the minimum.

7
00:00:30,516 --> 00:00:34,843
The FirstBank deal and loan growth
fed the margin, while fees were soft.

8
00:00:35,393 --> 00:00:41,437
As CFO Rob Reilly put it, we continue
to demonstrate strong momentum
across the franchise.

